course: dictionary
lesson: 2069
title: Conspiracy: a secret plan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A conspiracy is a secret plan made by a group of people to do something harmful or illegal. Look for clues in the words around it. Here, the words secret, group and harmful tell you what a conspiracy is.
explain: «Many online videos say scary things that are not true to get views; clickbait is a scary or exciting title made to get clicks, and a conspiracy theory is a false story about a secret plan.» A conspiracy theory is a story that says a secret group is behind something. The clues are false and secret plan.
explain: The word can also mean the act of planning such a thing: «They were found guilty of conspiracy». Try your meaning in the sentence: "They were found guilty of secret planning to do something harmful" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: A conspiracy is a secret plan by a group to do something harmful or illegal, such as «a conspiracy to rob the bank».
fact: In 1605 the Gunpowder Plot was a conspiracy to blow up Parliament. Guy Fawkes is remembered on Bonfire Night in the UK.
fact: A conspiracy theory is a belief that a secret group is behind events, often without good evidence.
fact: Good readers check claims against reliable evidence before they believe them.
fact: Useful phrases include «a conspiracy theory», «a conspiracy of silence» and «uncover a conspiracy».
exercise: «They were found guilty of conspiracy.» What does conspiracy mean here? | A bright light used in a theatre | A famous painting | *The act of planning something harmful or illegal in secret | A kind of music played at parties
exercise: What is a conspiracy theory? | A prize given to detectives | A video that always tells the truth | A plan to win a football match | *A belief that a secret group is behind events, often without good evidence
exercise: Mia says a conspiracy is just a fancy word for a surprise party. Why is she wrong? | It is a word for a holiday | It means exactly the same as a party | A surprise party is a conspiracy in every case | *A conspiracy is a secret plan to do something harmful or illegal
test: Which word means a secret plan to do something harmful or illegal, like «a conspiracy to rob the bank»? | *A conspiracy | A library book | A sunny day | A birthday party
test: The detective decided to uncover a conspiracy. What does uncover mean here? | Bury | Hide | Forget | *Discover
exam: Which is the best way to check a conspiracy theory before you believe it? | Ask a friend who likes it | Believe it if many people say it | *Check it against reliable evidence | Share it quickly to get views
